# Line endings are a CONTRACT here, not a style preference: the production CSP
# allows the inline splash script in public/index.html by its sha256 hash, and
# that hash is computed over the exact bytes the browser receives. A CRLF
# working copy (Windows default via core.autocrlf) hashes differently, so the
# browser would refuse to run the script and the lobby would flash on every
# load. LF everywhere keeps every checkout byte-identical to the container.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched by any of the above.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.onnx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
